{"title":"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all ordered triple of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250db015f4a06bd9445a939dfc3aa60667c1a4e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_2,a_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff5df3733efc9a8d1f28e033042a4d1d2d59f3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le a_1,a_2,a_3 \\le 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />. Each ordered triple in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> generates a sequence according to the rule <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca57c167f294147e5f0116256f0462e0f49187ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=a_{n-1}\\cdot | a_{n-2}-a_{n-3} |$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb6055493807459fe9b3d658e9683a25d1cd63bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Find the number of such sequences for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> for some index <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd93f79c3a76106e45c798db719656ea3bb581ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-2}=a_{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"14\" />. We proceed with casework, where overlap with the former cases are excluded.\n</p><p><b>Case 1: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50e91da2570c922e4f42381bba798c8ad45a81b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}=a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>There are clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b085668dbec5f7ac7ce468298ca36deca25cf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot 10=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" /> combinations.\n</p><p><b>Case 2: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be9e698f3eb154d5c15fe21f847539f32a610755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}=a_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>There are clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d42c119e316326c11f0a7c85780de9e7d36118f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\cdot 9=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" /> combinations.\n</p><p><b>Case 3: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/3/2c3f644f29d4cf5d3a55780c7376eef3289c3442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4}=a_{3}\\iff \\lvert a_{2}-a_{1}\\lvert =1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5e44e794fa93f2c01a4555f5ce4d87f8eaaf32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}=2,3,\\ldots, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" /> there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577f233ff970bde00137808bfa15c1e96df56f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f4cfa9819e2a179bb83a3fd27c8552927c79c29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}=1, 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577f233ff970bde00137808bfa15c1e96df56f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is fixed. In total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b48c7f138f6f0053edbf36695de547311879a5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\cdot 8\\cdot 2+9\\cdot 2=162$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"15\" /> combinations.\n</p><p><b>Case 4: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77b2f9e78af59dfc5938470a5d37b17942e294a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{5}=a_{4}\\iff \\lvert a_{3}-a_{2}\\lvert =1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5e44e794fa93f2c01a4555f5ce4d87f8eaaf32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}=2,3,\\ldots, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" /> there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577f233ff970bde00137808bfa15c1e96df56f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f4cfa9819e2a179bb83a3fd27c8552927c79c29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}=1, 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577f233ff970bde00137808bfa15c1e96df56f9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is fixed. In total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f8c1af15a57f3e6661471d282f4f2e8b151fe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\cdot 8\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 8=128$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"15\" /> combinations.\n</p><p><b>Case 5: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/3/4b3c12ffc65ce00f283dae0c49e3780f10785327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{6}=a_{5}\\iff \\lvert a_{4}-a_{3}\\lvert =1 \\iff a_{3}=1, \\lvert a_{2}-a_{1}\\rvert = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"420\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Note that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab016efa4709ea94520ed7836bb6ed72e06a4895.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" />, any multiple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/5/5154251020a06b2d05759559383f26d6881f56a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4}=k\\cdot a_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" /> never suffices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880b742603ee17717f2119a3ac9c98b04ee59a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lvert a_{4}-a_{3}\\rvert=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, as the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e19e31d36c74a0eaab359a4732189c9f3869923a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k-1)a_{3}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> has no integer solutions. Hence, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/5/4d51ead9ba528c0bb9ee1a1821c679229c76aab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{3}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> to achieve this case.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f614ab3d4e96a51808d7a02cc66ce57d1ad72138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}=3,4,\\ldots, 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab1dc0f8f63bab8f7f287b6511956e56bc074b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{2}=9,10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1da7198d9a79e0a6dc32e60162044ee0f726e4e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is fixed. In total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e94b9749fc5e335d088d2a3e4d4e880a0b0ca5e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot 6+2=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> combinations.\n</p><p><b>Case 6: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/666bae9bc9762d619428a463899767d39c81c792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{7}=a_{6}\\iff \\lvert a_{5}-a_{4}\\lvert =1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>By a similar observation from <b>Case 5</b>, this is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/7/857b2422046551526f0fa20b68a01a66c7bf6a06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{4}=1, \\lvert a_{3}-a_{2}\\rvert=2\\iff a_{3}=1, \\lvert a_{2}-a_{1}\\rvert=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"372\" height=\"20\" />. This implies our previous conditions is necessary for the cases beyond <b>Case 5</b>. Indeed, proceeding inductively, we see that \n\\begin{array}{c|c|c}\n\\text{Case} &amp; \\text{Condition} &amp; \\text{Overlap with:} \\\\ \\hline\n\\text{Case 6}  &amp; a_{3}=1, \\lvert a_{2}-a_{1}\\rvert=1 &amp; \\text{Case 3}\\\\\n\\text{Case 7}  &amp; a_{4}=1, \\lvert a_{3}-a_{2}\\rvert=1 &amp; \\text{Case 4}\\\\\n\\text{Case 8}  &amp; a_{5}=1, \\lvert a_{4}-a_{3}\\rvert=1 &amp; \\text{Case 5}\\\\\n\\text{Case 9}  &amp; a_{6}=1, \\lvert a_{5}-a_{4}\\rvert=1 &amp; \\text{Case 3}\\\\\n\\ldots &amp; \\ldots &amp;\\ldots\n\\end{array}\nThus, all possible sequences are discussed.\n</p><p>Therefore, the total of such sequences is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acae3c8f01b7657935004d0bbe7964aa5c413957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100+90+162+128+14=\\boxed{494}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"272\" height=\"25\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5d32b0a4d5ccd52f0b374c3367326848b4322d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=x, a_2=y, a_3=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"168\" height=\"11\" />. First note that if any absolute value equals 0, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />.\nAlso note that if at any position, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9b46cf986aa27bd43f8369b647654fa46c630a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=a_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"10\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/7457297cf546e4dbf95f0c7c6c692ee229f80f56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+2}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />.\nThen, if any absolute value equals 1, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />.\nTherefore, if either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f57bf351a54fd78c5484d4e1a5de7a4db1e23b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y-x|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/3/363b34f019f4a3d4063208244da9c6bd25f5ee86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z-y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> is less than or equal to 1, then that ordered triple meets the criteria.\nAssume that to be the only way the criteria is met.\nTo prove, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a74f4366c2ff8c526ebf60039f5cc685538103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y-x|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d9de67a49190f822718bf3ba10311a3359f291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z-y|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529c0a9b0d3ed6a9964d03f87d1f56c016e28f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4 \\ge 2z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/32093e9150596145dbfcc9af9247006371182374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5 \\ge 4z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a11880f18b44fbc2d98f6cc3b586eb92b4421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6 \\ge 4z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />.\nHowever, since the minimum values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5d34d49a7eb6afd4874d7bdaf23946dbf63cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/a/34ace040475607683853fcfd4960a8f7fa6678c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> are equal, there must be a scenario where the criteria was met that does not meet our earlier scenarios. Calculation shows that to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0abe3819a39769d432113f16183cc153d1490b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y-x|=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />. Again assume that any other scenario will not meet criteria.\nTo prove, divide the other scenarios into two cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf27b25b0af3fcd6657702aeb9fe135ba6623994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a74f4366c2ff8c526ebf60039f5cc685538103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y-x|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d9de67a49190f822718bf3ba10311a3359f291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z-y|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/b/f6b63fbe3df33472fedbcea74d28cd5a9c50d0f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y-x|&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/d/f0d9de67a49190f822718bf3ba10311a3359f291.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z-y|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.\nFor the first one, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529c0a9b0d3ed6a9964d03f87d1f56c016e28f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4 \\ge 2z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/32093e9150596145dbfcc9af9247006371182374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5 \\ge 4z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d796e3b1ccb7a204876ccaa6d46a3e9738b284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6 \\ge 8z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82dd8cd1404f4adb121bf6c0185f8569fca22b92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_7 \\ge 16z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" />, by which point we see that this function diverges.\nFor the second one, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f6b145661545479e2229bdd5873dbaeeb02e3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4 \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/1/d01ceb5a056902696dc89152f5e19ab40e202d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5 \\ge 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd702f0b0c872294542a71114d3571a2f8a99d1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6 \\ge 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189be5495945575c0e14f44ee2c7df8510c3f916.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_7 \\ge 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, by which point we see that this function diverges.\n</p><p><br />\nTherefore, the only scenarios where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb88988bde58a51f19f59c763ee7e64b140e96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" /> is when any of the following are met:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/f/a6fdec5cccf28759d872db34ddd06cc397a15ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y-x|&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> (280 options)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c5d41b209ade83b730358bce9ca8f3804463c10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z-y|&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" /> (280 options, 80 of which coincide with option 1)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0abe3819a39769d432113f16183cc153d1490b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y-x|=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />. (16 options, 2 of which coincide with either option 1 or option 2)\nAdding the total number of such ordered triples yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4cb4d605f2a00cd1ca6409ca78cca86f6add794.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$280+280-80+16-2=\\boxed{494}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"252\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the only way for a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to be produced at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is if either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633c0edf60e9e9ee0abfde883177e3dad2937523.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-1} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/910a53c5ee97fd0280880eaf1dca1d9cde74eedf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-2} = a_{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"10\" />. Since the first one will eventually get to the first three assuming that there is no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/0/910a53c5ee97fd0280880eaf1dca1d9cde74eedf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n-2} = a_{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"10\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, that is not possible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/5846539b4d2ae71a225920595c563315267f055a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 , a_2 , a_3 &gt;= 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/55536a619050d7186f5bfdef1b1d9d8c68fe08a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n - 2} = a_{n - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive numbers out of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/c/62cbb29712dd3ff4063c11fbe69453fdd3565038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 , a_2 , a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"66\" height=\"11\" /> are equal, then those cases work(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f92dfe245c114a14b4ff4336ab3e921b381d47e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{NOT}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />). This is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812b58ee69a5fdb8ef1de3c17cb138c1276d0989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\cdot 10 + 10 \\cdot 10 - 10 = 190$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"212\" height=\"14\" /> by PIE. \n</p><p>Now, note that if any of the first three numbers have difference of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have another working case. First, we calculate how many there are given exactly one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf15de06961094052da6ef3f061596ddb4745737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"11\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d153f9254df8db0e09a0dcfe2e284df6bd03dc9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2,a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"11\" /> have difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers such that the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> have difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> permutations work(assuming the numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692e3bee67c91837acbdcf63862b3b3c94366f28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/8/2185212a94cf47d36ed6aae0d26e15f7b236a510.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-y| = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />): <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daac5e5656708db09b9e0ce06edc14cf08bb9a9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,x,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa0cae6e1e2c8f4db887a707d816b930856d674f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z,x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/e/7be57b26012c87ba21b582852f8a706a30b3cb27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z,y,x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"11\" />. If the two consecutive numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then the last number has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possiblities: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb16a46e3efcfffb3faa238032676a6976c7363e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,5,6,\\cdots , 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />. This is symmetric for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. If the consecutive numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/e/4be7d887e6bcd06ca2b731dbf69baa75c9ade475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3),\\cdots , (8,9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> minus the numbers themselves and the numbers directly above and below). Note that we are not counting any cases already counted in the first case. Therefore, this case gives you <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d89e4450d4bd33baa1fb349389b65a8a8488ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4(7 + 6 * 7 + 7) = 224$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />. Now we consider the case that there both adjacent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />s have increments of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da18dcb589a57b960f533e5528442bd13ec5a88e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[+1 , +1 \\rightarrow 8\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b2e49c5542143e186e2b3ec120cf9aead98e3a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-1 , -1 \\rightarrow 8\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16ad5eb8caa8bec32f0772c024010c8e77d1ce0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[+1 , -1 \\rightarrow 9\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/30937ecd233d9dfdb2d698dcfbf5d5f8764d1b86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-1 , +1 \\rightarrow 9\\]\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> Therefore this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341dd2eb1fdbf9b6ab8321c10aef185e1f5cc17e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$224 + 8 + 8 + 9 + 9 = 258$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"203\" height=\"14\" />. However, note that we have to add the case where you have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive numbers in arrangement such that only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive numbers have difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/2/8b2e23218bd88174fcde5f999ca7b2a363792a2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,3,2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> is one such triple. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triples of consecutive numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ways to arrange each one(e.x: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ce03fc7a2b737abad13cc287be07dc74bd0794f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,3,2);(3,1,2);(2,1,3);(2,3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" />). This adds on 32 working cases, so this case gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c31f63e899ec610bba887d02ffe3451a4e35e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$258 + 32 = 290$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Note that there is an ultraspecial(Yes, I know that's not a word) case where we generate a pair of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> that have difference one. This can only happen if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/d/eddca35a35c09c5d25dd7584c771a65d90e762fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> have difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cases(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e16f27d4883ec2858065d5a4bd12119549067030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 * 8$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and then subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because of the cases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d068508de46e9e120e9b828f3ab9db84eb1faee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,1,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbf67a2a0d66d599b9215d2f57541a7b9732c3b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,2,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />).\n</p><p>Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d73cddb67f167c84f93dc3784e0a58b66044c041.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$190 + 290 + 14 = \\boxed{494}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"180\" height=\"23\" />.\nSolution by hyxue\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/nxieVbkk0jY\">https://youtu.be/nxieVbkk0jY</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I\" title=\"2015 AIME I\">2015 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2015\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Pro